import BlogLayout from "../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
---

<BlogLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  heroTitle="Editorial Policy"
  heroSubtitle="Last updated: November 24, 2026"
>
  <section class="card page-card">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        AITech8 is an independent guide to AI tools. This policy
        explains how we choose what to cover, how we evaluate tools,
        and how we keep our recommendations independent from commercial
        relationships.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Choose What to Cover</h2>
      <p>
        We cover AI tools that readers ask about, tools with a new
        release or a meaningful pricing or feature change, and tools
        that solve a real workflow problem. Coverage is decided by the
        editorial team based on reader demand and usefulness. Vendors
        cannot pay to be covered, and no tool is covered only because
        it offers an affiliate commission.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Evaluate Tools</h2>
      <p>
        Every evaluation is built from primary sources: the vendor’s
        official documentation, official pricing pages, API
        documentation, and published product changelogs. Prices,
        plan limits, and feature lists are cross-checked against the
        vendor’s official pages at the time of writing, and each
        article shows its publication or update date because prices
        and features change. Where tools are compared side by side,
        the comparison uses the same criteria for every tool in the
        comparison.
      </p>
      <h2>No Fabricated Testing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not claim hands-on testing we did not perform. When a
        tool was tried directly, the article says so and describes
        what was tested. When an evaluation is based on official
        documentation and published sources, the article says that
        instead. We never invent test results, benchmarks, speed
        measurements, or user quotes. If a claim cannot be verified
        against an official source, we do not publish it as fact.
      </p>
      <h2>AI Assistance and Human Review</h2>
      <p>
        Drafts may be produced with AI assistance. Every article is
        reviewed and fact-checked by a human editor against primary
        sources before publication, and articles that fail that check
        are revised or not published. AI output is never published
        without human verification.
      </p>
      <h2>Accuracy and Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Prices, limits, and features change frequently, so an article
        may become outdated even when it was accurate on its
        publication date. When we find an error, or a reader reports
        one, we correct it promptly and update the article’s update
        date. Significant corrections are noted in the article. To
        report an error, contact us at{" "}
        <a href="mailto:hello@aitech8.com">hello@aitech8.com</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Affiliate Links and Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you sign up
        for or purchase a product through one, this site may earn a
        commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate links are marked
        with rel="sponsored nofollow" and disclosed in our{" "}
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Affiliate
        relationships do not influence which tools we cover, how we
        rank them, or what we recommend. We do not publish undisclosed
        sponsored reviews: any sponsored content, if it ever appears,
        will be clearly labeled as sponsored.
      </p>
      <h2>Authorship</h2>
      <p>
        Articles are published under the AITech8 editorial team. We do
        not invent author identities, biographies, or credentials, and
        we do not attribute to any person work they did not do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BlogLayout>
